repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wekempf/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wekempf/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wekempf/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-17T14:47:01Z","updated_at":"2026-03-17T14:47:01Z","body":"Not supporting this doesn't even make sense. If you're using a prompt/agent that's restricted tools to not include the ability to use scripts, but the skill has scripts, what even happens?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/4075533546/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/4075629293","html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/14131#issuecomment-4075629293","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/14131","id":4075629293,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJYd5Dc7y7Srt","user":{"login":"wekempf","id":3430823,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MzA4MjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3430823?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wekempf","html_url":"https://github.com/wekempf","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wekempf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wekempf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wekempf/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wekempf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wekempf/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wekempf/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wekempf/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wekempf/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wekempf/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-17T14:58:48Z","updated_at":"2026-03-17T14:58:48Z","body":"Some questions to be answered:\n\n1. Is it bad that it's `allowed-tools` here, but `tools` in prompts and agents?\n2. The VS Code experience needs to be compatible with \"cross tool\" skill definitions if skills are a \"standard\". Since tools are unique to each \"agentic tool\" (Copilot, Claude CLI, Pi, etc.), the only way this seems to be doable is to:\n    - Not put squiggles under unrecognized tool names, as they may be the name used by other agentic tools.\n    - When using the UI to configure tools it should not remove any unrecognized tools, or at least the UI should have a way to toggle this behavior.\n\nOn 2 above, the other option is to get *all* other agentic tools to standardize on tool names. With Copilot's history of changing tool names on a whim, I'd say good luck with that ;).","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/4075629293/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]}